    "reading": {
        "body": "Lambda's API registered healthy responses only 28.7 percent of the time across 87 observations, making it a severe outlier against a field where every other measured provider exceeded 96 percent uptime over the same window starting August 14, 2026.\n\nEleven of the twelve providers in the dataset sat between 96.8 and 100 percent, a remarkably tight band. Five providers, AssemblyAI, Cohere, Deepgram, Groq, and Stability AI, recorded a perfect 100 percent across their full observation counts. The clustering suggests that, for most providers, API availability has become a solved operational problem, at least over this particular measurement window.\n\nLambda's result stands apart enough to warrant caution in interpreting it. Its observation count of 87 is slightly lower than the 93 recorded for most peers, which could reflect monitoring gaps rather than, or in addition to, genuine outages. The data does not distinguish between causes, whether infrastructure, power, networking, or measurement error. What it does confirm is that Lambda's API was unreachable or unhealthy during a large fraction of the checks taken, and any workload depending on it during this period would have experienced frequent failures. The data covers roughly two and a half weeks and twelve providers, so it does not speak to longer-term trends or to providers outside this set.",
